>mit meiner Muttersprache</i>."}]}, {"id": "Mein Bruder spielt Fußball", "de": "Mein Bruder spielt Fußball", "en": "my brother plays football", "lesson": 1, "chunks": ["mein Bruder", "spielt", "Fußball"], "finite": "spielt", "accepted": [["mein Bruder", "spielt", "Fußball"], ["Fußball", "spielt", "mein Bruder"]], "marked": [1], "derived": null, "distractors": [{"text": "spielen", "replaces": "spielt", "why": "<b>spielen</b> goes with <i>wir or sie (plural)</i>. Here say <b>spielt</b>."}, {"text": "meinem Bruder", "replaces": "mein Bruder", "why": "The sentence is about <b>mein Bruder</b>. You only say <i>meinem Bruder</i> after words like <i>mit</i>: <i>mit meinem Bruder</i>."}]}, {"id": "Meine Schwester spielt Tennis", "de": "Meine Schwester spielt Tennis", "en": "my sister plays tennis", "lesson": 1, "chunks": ["meine Schwester", "spielt", "Tennis"], "finite": "spielt", "accepted": [["meine Schwester", "spielt", "Tennis"], ["Tennis", "spielt", "meine Schwester"]], "marked": [1], "derived": null, "distractors": [{"text": "spielen", "replaces": "spielt", "why": "<b>spielen</b> goes with <i>wir or sie (plural)</i>. Here say <b>spielt</b>."}, {"text": "meiner Schwester", "replaces": "meine Schwester", "why": "The sentence is about <b>meine Schwester</b>. You only say <i>meiner Schwester</i> after words like <i>mit</i>: <i>mit meiner Schwester</i>."}]}, {"id": "Mein Sohn spielt Tischtennis", "de": "Mein Sohn spielt Tischtennis", "en": "my son plays table tennis", "lesson": 1, "chunks": ["mein Sohn", "spielt", "Tischtennis"], "finite": "spielt", "accepted": [["mein Sohn", "spielt", "Tischtennis"], ["Tischtennis", "spielt", "mein Sohn"]], "marked": [1], "derived": null, "distractors": [{"text": "spielen", "replaces": "spielt", "why": "<b>spielen</b> goes with <i>wir or sie (plural)</i>. Here say <b>spielt</b>."}, {"text": "meinem Sohn", "replaces": "mein Sohn", "why": "The sentence is about <b>mein Sohn</b>. You only say <i>meinem Sohn</i> after words like <i>mit</i>: <i>mit meinem Sohn</i>."}]}, {"id": "Wir haben eine Tochter", "de": "Wir haben eine Tochter", "en": "we have a daughter", "lesson": 1, "chunks": ["wir", "haben", "eine Tochter"], "finite": "haben", "accepted": [["wir", "haben", "eine Tochter"], ["eine Tochter", "haben", "wir"]], "marked": [1], "derived": null, "distractors": [{"text": "hat", "replaces": "haben", "why": "<b>hat</b> goes with <i>er or sie</i>. Here say <b>haben</b>."}, {"text": "keine Tochter", "replaces": "eine Tochter", "why": "<i>keine Tochter</i> means you have no daughter. The English says you have one, so <b>eine Tochter</b>."}]}, {"id": "Meine Mutter spielt Gitarre", "de": "Meine Mutter spielt Gitarre", "en": "my mother plays guitar", "lesson": 1, "chunks": ["meine Mutter", "spielt", "Gitarre"], "finite": "spielt", "accepted": [["meine Mutter", "spielt", "Gitarre"], ["Gitarre", "spielt", "meine Mutter"]], "marked": [1], "derived": null, "distractors": [{"text": "spielen", "replaces": "spielt", "why": "<b>spielen</b> goes with <i>wir or sie (plural)</i>. Here say <b>spielt</b>."}, {"text": "meiner Mutter", "replaces": "meine Mutter", "why": "The sentence is about <b>meine Mutter</b>. You only say <i>meiner Mutter</i> after words like <i>mit</i>: <i>mit meiner Mutter</i>."}]}, {"id": "Mein Vater singt im Chor", "de": "Mein Vater singt im Chor", "en": "my father sings in the choir", "lesson": 1, "chunks": ["mein Vater", "singt", "im Chor"], "finite": "singt", "accepted": [["mein Vater", "singt", "im Chor"], ["im Chor", "singt", "mein Vater"]], "marked": [], "derived": null, "distractors": [{"text": "singst", "replaces": "singt", "why": "<b>singst</b> goes with <i>du</i>. Here say <b>singt</b>."}, {"text": "in den Chor", "replaces": "im Chor", "why": "<i>in den Chor</i> means going into it. He is already there and singing, so <b>im Chor</b>."}]}, {"id": "Die Eltern wohnen in der Stadt", "de": "Die Eltern wohnen in der Stadt", "en": "the parents live in the city", "lesson": 1, "chunks": ["die Eltern",