th <i>du</i>. Here say <b>ist</b>."}, {"text": "sind", "replaces": "ist", "why": "<b>sind</b> goes with <i>wir or sie (plural)</i>. Here say <b>ist</b>."}]}, {"id": "Er arbeitet als Kellner", "de": "Er arbeitet als Kellner", "en": "he works as a waiter", "lesson": 1, "chunks": ["er", "arbeitet", "als Kellner"], "finite": "arbeitet", "accepted": [["er", "arbeitet", "als Kellner"], ["als Kellner", "arbeitet", "er"]], "marked": [], "derived": null, "distractors": [{"text": "arbeitest", "replaces": "arbeitet", "why": "<b>arbeitest</b> goes with <i>du</i>. Here say <b>arbeitet</b>."}, {"text": "arbeite", "replaces": "arbeitet", "why": "<b>arbeite</b> goes with <i>ich</i>. Here say <b>arbeitet</b>."}]}, {"id": "Der Nachbar hört laut Musik", "de": "Der Nachbar hört laut Musik", "en": "the neighbour listens to loud music", "lesson": 1, "chunks": ["der Nachbar", "hört", "laut", "Musik"], "finite": "hört", "accepted": [["der Nachbar", "hört", "laut", "Musik"], ["Musik", "hört", "der Nachbar", "laut"]], "marked": [1], "derived": null, "distractors": [{"text": "hörst", "replaces": "hört", "why": "<b>hörst</b> goes with <i>du</i>. Here say <b>hört</b>."}, {"text": "dem Nachbarn", "replaces": "der Nachbar", "why": "The sentence is about <b>der Nachbar</b>. You only say <i>dem Nachbarn</i> after words like <i>mit</i>: <i>mit dem Nachbarn</i>."}]}, {"id": "Am Abend ist es heiß", "de": "Am Abend ist es heiß", "en": "in the evening it is hot", "lesson": 1, "chunks": ["am Abend", "ist", "es", "heiß"], "finite": "ist", "accepted": [["am Abend", "ist", "es", "heiß"], ["es", "ist", "am Abend", "heiß"]], "marked": [], "derived": null, "distractors": [{"text": "sind", "replaces": "ist", "why": "<b>sind</b> goes with <i>wir or sie (plural)</i>. Here say <b>ist</b>."}, {"text": "bist", "replaces": "ist", "why": "<b>bist</b> goes with <i>du</i>. Here say <b>ist</b>."}]}, {"id": "Ich komme aus Kasachstan", "de": "Ich komme aus Kasachstan", "en": "I come from Kazakhstan", "lesson": 1, "chunks": ["ich", "komme", "aus Kasachstan"], "finite": "komme", "accepted": [["ich", "komme", "aus Kasachstan"], ["aus Kasachstan", "komme", "ich"]], "marked": [], "derived": null, "distractors": [{"text": "kommst", "replaces": "komme", "why": "<b>kommst</b> goes with <i>du</i>. Here say <b>komme</b>."}, {"text": "in Kasachstan", "replaces": "aus Kasachstan", "why": "<i>in Kasachstan</i> means you are there now. To say where you are from, use <b>aus</b>."}]}, {"id": "Ich buchstabiere den Namen", "de": "Ich buchstabiere den Namen", "en": "I spell the name", "lesson": 1, "chunks": ["ich", "buchstabiere", "den Namen"], "finite": "buchstabiere", "accepted": [["ich", "buchstabiere", "den Namen"], ["den Namen", "buchstabiere", "ich"]], "marked": [1], "derived": null, "distractors": [{"text": "buchstabierst", "replaces": "buchstabiere", "why": "<b>buchstabierst</b> goes with <i>du</i>. Here say <b>buchstabiere</b>."}, {"text": "dem Namen", "replaces": "den Namen", "why": "After <b>buchstabiere</b>, <i>dem</i> becomes <b>den</b>: <i>Ich buchstabiere den Namen</i>."}]}, {"id": "Ich schreibe die Telefonnummer", "de": "Ich schreibe die Telefonnummer", "en": "I write down the phone number", "lesson": 1, "chunks": ["ich", "schreibe", "die Telefonnummer"], "finite": "schreibe", "accepted": [["ich", "schreibe", "die Telefonnummer"], ["die Telefonnummer", "schreibe", "ich"]], "marked": [1], "derived": null, "distractors": [{"text": "schreibst", "replaces": "schreibe", "why": "<b>schreibst</b> goes with <i>du</i>. Here say <b>schreibe</b>."}, {"text": "der Telefonnummer", "replaces": "die Telefonnummer", "why": "After <b>schreibe</b>, <i>der</i> becomes <b>die</b>: <i>Ich schreibe die Telefonnummer</i>."}]}, {"id": "Ich lese ein Buch", "de": "Ich lese ein Buch", "en": "I read a book", "lesson": 1, "chunks": ["ich", "lese", "ein Buch"], "finite": "lese", "accepted": [["ich", "lese", "ein Buch"], ["ein Buch", "lese", "ich"]], "marked": [1], "derived": null, "distractors": [{"text": "liest", "replaces": "lese", "why": "<b>liest</b> goes with <i>du, er or sie</i>. Here say <b>lese</b>."}, {"text": "kein Buch", "replaces": "ein Buch", "why": "<i>kein Buch</i> means you are not reading a book. The English says you are, so <b>ein Buch</b>."}]}, {"id": "Ich habe eine Frage", "de": "Ich habe eine Frage", "en": "I have a question", "lesson": 1, "chunks": ["ich", "habe", "eine Frage"], "finite": "habe", "accepted": [["ich", "habe", "eine Frage"], ["eine Frage", "habe", "ich"]], "marked": [1], "derived": null, "distractors": [{"text": "hast", "replaces": "habe", "why": "<b>hast</b> goes with <i>du</i>. Here say <b>habe</b>."}, {"text": "keine Frage", "replaces": "eine Frage", "why": "<i>keine Frage</i> means you have no question. The English says you have one, so <b>eine Frage</b>."}]}, {"id": "Ich habe keine Frage", "de": "Ich habe keine Frage", "en": "I do not have a question", "lesson": 1, "chunks": ["ich", "habe", "keine", "Frage"], "finite": "habe", "accepted": [["ich", "habe", "keine", "Frage"], ["Frage", "habe", "ich", "keine"]], "marked": [1], "derived": "Ich habe eine Frage", "distractors": [{"text": "hast", "replaces": "habe", "why": "<b>hast</b> goes with <i>du</i>. Here say <b>habe</b>."}, {"text": "nicht", "replaces": "keine", "why": "A noun with <i>eine</i> is negated with <b>keine</b>, not <i>nicht</i>."}]}, {"id": "Das ist eine Person", "de": "Das ist eine Person", "en": "that is a person", "lesson": 1, "chunks": ["das", "ist", "eine Person"], "finite": "ist", "accepted": [["das", "ist", "eine Person"], ["eine Person", "ist", "das"]], "marked": [1], "derived": null, "distractors": [{"text": "sind", "replaces": "ist", "why": "<b>sind</b> goes with <i>wir or sie (plural)</i>. Here say <b>ist</b>."}, {"text": "keine Person", "replaces": "eine Person", "why": "<i>keine Person</i> means it is not a person. The English says it is one, so <b>eine Person</b>."}]}, {"id": "Die Leute wohnen hier", "de": "Die Leute wohnen hier", "en": "the people live here",